IMPORT prelude

-- Statutory Bodies and Government Companies (Protection of Secrecy) Act 1983 (Singapore) -- which organisations the Act protects
-- (s 2 and the Schedule), the duty of secrecy on their members, officers, employees and agents and its two exceptions (s 3(1), (2)),
-- the penalty (s 3(3)), the Public Prosecutor's written consent to prosecute (s 4), and who may amend the Schedule (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/7/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SBGCPSA1983.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 17 of 2026 wef 01/07/2026 (deleting Schedule item 33); S 120/2026 wef 18/03/2026 is also annotated.
-- THE SCHEDULE TABLE IS COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT: each body was matched to its establishing Act by item number and order
-- of appearance, not by line position.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0219 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is five sections and a Schedule, so the whole operative text is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (short
-- title); the Schedule is encoded only for a SAMPLE of its listed bodies plus PSA Corporation Limited and its subsidiaries, with some
-- unlisted organisations for contrast; the secrecy provisions of the bodies' own establishing Acts (not read); what makes a document
-- "secret or confidential" (the Act does not define it -- left to the facts).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Statutory Bodies and Government Companies (Protection of Secrecy) Act 1983`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- specified organisations`

-- s 2: "'specified organisation' means a statutory body or a Government company which is specified in the Schedule."
-- Schedule Part 1 (statutory bodies) lists, among others: 4 Central Provident Fund Board; 5A Communicable Diseases Agency; 10A
-- Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore; 13 Housing and Development Board; 15 Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore; 18 Land
-- Transport Authority of Singapore; 19 Majlis Ugama Islam, Singapura; 21 Monetary Authority of Singapore; 22 National Environment
-- Agency; 24 People's Association; 26 Public Utilities Board; 27 Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board; 31 Skills and
-- Workforce Development Agency; 32 Urban Redevelopment Authority. Items 3 and 33 are "[Deleted ...]".
-- Schedule Part 2 (Government companies): "PSA Corporation Limited and its subsidiary corporations." -- the only entry.
-- The unlisted organisations below are NOT in the Schedule as deposited; the Act does not reach them.
DECLARE Organisation IS ONE OF
    `Central Provident Fund Board`
    `Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore`
    `Housing and Development Board`
    `Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `Land Transport Authority of Singapore`
    `Majlis Ugama Islam Singapura`
    `Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `National Environment Agency`
    `People's Association`
    `Public Utilities Board`
    `Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board`
    `Skills and Workforce Development Agency`
    `Urban Redevelopment Authority`
    `PSA Corporation Limited`
    `a subsidiary corporation of PSA Corporation Limited`
    `Health Sciences Authority`
    `Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority`
    `a Government ministry`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the organisation` IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a specified organisation` IF
    CONSIDER `the organisation`
    WHEN `Health Sciences Authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Government ministry` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- protection of secrecy`

-- s 3(1): "A person who is or has been a member or an officer, employee or agent of a specified organisation must not, without
-- authority of that organisation, disclose to any other person any secret or confidential document or information which the person
-- has obtained or to which the person has access by virtue of the person's position as such member, officer, employee or agent."
-- (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure of any document or information -- (a) for the purpose of the performance of
-- his or her duties or functions by any member, officer, employee or agent of a specified organisation; or (b) which is lawfully
-- required or authorised to be disclosed by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions of any written law." [5/2018]
-- (3): a contravention of (1) is an offence -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months
-- or to both".
--
-- "is or has been": a FORMER member, officer, employee or agent is bound; the duty has no end date.
-- Only DISCLOSURE is caught -- not use -- and only by the insider; the Act creates no offence for the person who receives it.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `the organisation` IS AN Organisation
    `the discloser is or has been a member, officer, employee or agent of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained or accessed by virtue of that position` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document or information is secret or confidential` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the organisation authorised the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for performing the duties or functions of a member, officer, employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required or authorised by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) reaches the disclosure` IF
        `is a specified organisation` (`the disclosure`'s `the organisation`)
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the discloser is or has been a member, officer, employee or agent of it`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `obtained or accessed by virtue of that position`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the document or information is secret or confidential`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `the organisation authorised the disclosure`)

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2) excepts the disclosure` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `for performing the duties or functions of a member, officer, employee or agent`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required or authorised by a court`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by written law`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under s 3(3)` IF
        `s 3(1) reaches the disclosure` `the disclosure`
    AND (NOT `s 3(2) excepts the disclosure` `the disclosure`)

-- s 3(3) maxima. Fine and imprisonment may BOTH be imposed ("or to both").
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS 2000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 12

GIVEN `fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER, `imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within s 3(3)` IF
        `fine in dollars` AT LEAST 0
    AND `fine in dollars` AT MOST `the maximum fine in dollars`
    AND `imprisonment in months` AT LEAST 0
    AND `imprisonment in months` AT MOST `the maximum imprisonment in months`

§§ `4 -- consent for prosecution`

-- s 4: "A prosecution must not be instituted under this Act except with the written consent of the Public Prosecutor." [15/2010]
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `the consent is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented` AND `the consent is in writing`

§§ `5 -- amendment of the Schedule`

-- s 5: "The President may, by notification in the Gazette, amend the Schedule."
DECLARE Amender IS ONE OF
    `the President by notification in the Gazette`
    `a Minister by order`
    `the specified organisation itself`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Amender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may amend the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the President by notification in the Gazette` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
